hello my name is Juan Celestino yellow  and I am a product manager for  continuous integration continuous  delivery on Google Cloud today we'll be  talking about an exciting new feature  container registry vulnerability  scanning scanning your images for known  vulnerabilities is an important step in  securing your cic the pipeline  vulnerability scanning helps you  identify and address vulnerabilities in  images stored in Google container  registry in turn this enables you to  prioritize patching your images to  address these vulnerabilities determine  whether your environment is affected by  a newly discovered vulnerabilities and  ensure that your images are up-to-date  and protected against the latest threats  first enable the container and analysis  API to use the vulnerability scanner  once enabled it will automatically scan  the container images you have stored in  container registry it uses data from  vulnerability databases for the  supported distributions after an image  is scanned you can see that list of  vulnerabilities found under severity we  are a cloud console the command-line  interface and vulnerability scanners  api's also the vulnerability status of  previously scanned images is  automatically updated when new  vulnerabilities are reported to the  source databases to learn more about a  specific vulnerability in an image click  on it to go to the detailed view using  this information you can find and get a  patch version of the affected container  image if no vulnerabilities are found  for an image it will have a green check  mark with nan found in the  vulnerabilities column you can apply  additional security to your CI CD  process with binary authorization setup  policies to ensure that only container  images that meet your acceptance  criteria can be used in deployments  so to recap vulnerability scanner helps  you secure your CI CD process by  continuously identifying vulnerabilities  in your container images you can use  this information to decide what images  need to be patched  learn more check out documentation for  container registry vulnerability  scanning thanks for watching
 

